  "classification": "Postprocessing-only correction for a factor-of-two denominator defect in the FP64 secant output of runner-001. Raw arrays, report, and manifest remain immutable. No constitutive/solver/source change and no numerical replay rerun.",
  "derivation": {
    "FP64_secant_bug": "runner lines 306 and 316 divide by epsilon only. Since symmetric path difference is 2*epsilon, raw FP64 secants are 2x derivatives. Correction is raw stored FP64 secant / 2; no root/state/branch/tolerance changes.",
    "MP_secant": "runner subtracts side stresses and divides by 2*epsilon, therefore epsilon-path derivative.",
    "assembly": "stress derivative is transformed by captured per-tet material frames, passed through captured inverse-rest and volume element force, gathered by exact tet connectivity; residual derivative is dt*internal_force_derivative - mass*captured_delta_v. Correcting stress derivative halves only the internal-force term; mass action is unchanged.",
    "captured_perturbation": "F_plus/minus = F0 +/- epsilon*dt*H on all 1920 paper+glue tets.",
    "center_IFT": "runner uses F0 +/- h*H and divides stress difference by 2h, producing dP/ds for F0+sH; epsilon-path target is dt*dP/ds."
  },
